        "text": "interacting with them; Invoke-WebRequest . We\u2019ll go on to look at Application Programming\nInterfaces ( APIs ). We\u2019ll talk about the dominant type of API in use today \u2013 Representational\nState Transfer ( REST ). Once we\u2019ve got a good grip on that and the tool we can use to work with it,\nInvoke-RestMethod , we\u2019ll look at some of the ways of exchanging information with web services\nusing JavaScript Object Notation ( JSON ), and the tools we use to convert JSON data into PowerShell\nobjects, and vice versa. Finally, we\u2019ll tackle a short exercise.\nThis chapter will give us the basic techniques we\u2019ll need for some of the work we\u2019ll do in later chapters\nof the book and build on some of the work we did in the last chapter. We\u2019ll see that those techniques\napply to data on the web as well.\nIn this chapter we are going to cover the following main topics:\n\u2022I Working with HTTP\n\u2022I Getting to grips with APIs\n\u2022I Working with REST\n\u2022I Working with JSON\nPowerShell and the Web \u2013 HTTP, REST, and JSON\n166",
